Transitive dependencies of Next.js that are not shipped in the site
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The workspace is built with Next.js (MIT) as a static export. Two packages that
Next.js installs carry licenses other than MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD or ISC. Neither
is part of the built site (apps/workspace/out/).

- @img/sharp-libvips-* (LGPL-3.0-or-later): the libvips binaries of sharp
  (Apache-2.0), an optional dependency of Next.js for image optimization. Unused:
  next.config.ts sets `images.unoptimized`, so sharp never runs.
  https://github.com/lovell/sharp-libvips
- caniuse-lite (CC-BY-4.0): browser support data, read at build time by
  Browserslist and Next.js. Data from caniuse.com by Alexis Deveria.
  https://github.com/browserslist/caniuse-lite
